  {
   "key": "0x20..0x27",
   "name": "non-specific EOI",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "513-522"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "555-573"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "582-584"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A non-specific EOI resets the highest in-service bit, which in the fully nested mode is the last level acknowledged.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "564-571",
       "sha": "df70e692109d21ec37ce039a1379f55e0ca74fe82f4ceb111ff1ca04920e21c2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A non-specific EOI is OCW2 with EOI = 1, SL = 0 and R = 0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "572-573",
       "sha": "72ee31fafc7a6e09f78f328769ee95f7d70f2955dc3b2fafa2a5486f40ced976"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "bits 7-5",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "R, SL and EOI control the rotate and end of interrupt modes; L2 L1 L0 give the level acted upon when SL is active.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "513-520",
       "sha": "4044df298f2ba0334ddab6ded3b8f9c75731c4e07dadb4980c83e635354b19f1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "when",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The in-service bit is reset by an EOI command issued before returning from a service routine, or automatically in AEOI mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "555-560",
       "sha": "f203a2ffb1a8c8e07d7345dd7523aca7b1f4d56032ebdfe64857c1a94e40846d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "when",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In cascade mode an EOI command must be issued twice, once for the master and once for the corresponding slave.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "561-563",
       "sha": "1231b13b7ba76d9c1c163ba732ff409afc2f341e72d586ad666d231d58e909ff"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "when",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "An in-service bit masked by an IMR bit is not cleared by a non-specific EOI in the special mask mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8259A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "582-584",
       "sha": "93bcffbbdc8e3b7522f173c007da4f99371f5c0fd4727cbd5f3786ac91fd576c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "when",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "6",
     "text": "A non-specific EOI scans from the priority base and tests only the in-service bits, never the mask bits, so a masked in-service bit is cleared too.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/pic8259.cpp",
       "lines": "288",
       "sha": "fd7a83fa35885c8b9aeb83311bf2bb51a488c1be1f832c7d9b26d11540464419"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/pic8259.cpp",
       "lines": "290",
       "sha": "1655dccbccbb4d8970e6f2e9836c6dc8ab39e416db4aee2c777fcf480b9e281f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "201",
     "on": "when",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "6",
     "text": "A non-specific EOI is carried out whenever a level is in service; the condition does not look at the mask or the special mask mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/pic.cpp",
       "lines": "279",
       "sha": "af5f7248bfd8d2dcd26eb727db09fe0acc7517b96e21766dca84dff227050fa1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "202",
     "on": "bits 7-5",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "3",
     "text": "Rotate commands are not supported: the R bit only logs a message and the EOI is carried out.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/pic.cpp",
       "lines": "272",
       "sha": "72e6eddd766f5a7f81925bc2b8be7fa1c3f4e8aa09ebff9e04e80760657444c3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
